SELECT '125c339c-f3bf-70ce-8650-4d70b0bd50c0', 'cac9fc11-fb32-751b-ba07-f04d783ab37a', 'Reading Complex Declarations', 'Reading Complex Declarations', 'C declarations mirror usage: int *a[3] says “*a[i] is an int”. Decode any declaration with the right-left rule — start at the name, go right, then left, and jump out of parentheses.
Find the identifier
Start at the name being declared.
Go right
[N] → “array of N”, (…) → “function taking … returning”. Stop at a ) or the end.
Go left
* → “pointer to”, const → “const”. Stop at a (.
Jump out
Leave the parentheses and repeat right-then-left until you reach the base type.
Declaration	Meaning
